        "Andreas Wallraff",
        "Robert J. Schoelkopf"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit QED made strong, controllable light-matter interaction in superconducting circuits a reproducible new platform for fundamental quantum optics and quantum information.",
        "attribution": "Blais supplied the decisive theoretical framework; Wallraff and Schoelkopf were central to its experimental realization and development.",
        "maturity": "The physics has been independently reproduced and is now foundational to superconducting quantum science.",
        "uncertainties": [
