        "Hidetoshi Katori",
        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks transformed precision measurement through an exceptionally clean and powerful realization of atomic timekeeping.",
        "attribution": "Katori originated the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept, while Ye made major pioneering experimental advances.",
        "maturity": "Performance, reproducibility, and scientific consequences are established across laboratories.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The ultimate division of credit among the wider clock community requires careful review."
        ]
      }
    },
