        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological-insulator framework revealed a new organizing principle for electronic quantum matter.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele developed the key theory, and Molenkamp led a pivotal experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "The phenomena and their topological interpretation are well established.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The relationship to previous recognition of topological phases and the full experimental credit requires assessment."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
