        "nobel_worthiness": "Rydberg blockade made large, programmable arrays of interacting atoms an exceptionally versatile quantum many-body platform.",
        "attribution": "Saffman supplied central blockade and gate concepts, while Browaeys and Lukin drove influential experimental realizations.",
        "maturity": "Rapid independent progress demonstrates robust control and substantial scientific reach.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Long-term maturity and the allocation of priority in a broad field remain less settled than for older candidates."
        ]
      }
